+
+Earlier attempts and what refuted them (do not repeat a refuted hypothesis):
+{self._attempt_memory()}
+
+Current diff:
+{current_diff if current_diff.strip() else '(empty)'}
+
+Instructions:
+- The reference is the source of truth for the problem definition. Find the smallest failing input above, trace both programs by hand on it,
+  and identify the exact discrepancy. If the reference itself looks wrong by the statement, fix the reference (files in {oracle_dir}) instead.
+- Do not trust a formula validated only on tiny inputs. Replace it with a correct algorithm whose agreement with the reference holds on the largest domain the brute force covers.
+- Fix the solution file with the editor tool (`edit` or `create`, which overwrites).
+- Re-run the differential test yourself: run the solution on the failing input with bash, and run `python3 {oracle_dir}/gen_small.py SEED` for several seeds to compare against the reference.
+- Do not write helper scripts with bash heredocs; write them with the editor tool.
+- Do not reply with text only; finish only after the fix is on disk and verified.
+"""
+            history = chat_with_agent(repair_msg, model=self.code_model, msg_history=[], logging=safe_log)
+            summary = self._clip(self._last_assistant_text(history), 2000)
+            first_fail = report.split("=== Failing case", 2)
+            first_fail_text = ("=== Failing case" + first_fail[1]) if len(first_fail) > 1 else "(see report)"
+            self.attempt_log.append(
+                f"Round {round_idx}: differential failures {n_fail}. First failing case:\n{self._clip(first_fail_text, 800)}\n"
+                f"Agent's stated hypothesis and fix:\n{summary or '(no summary)'}"
+            )
+            safe_log(f"[differential round {round_idx}] repair chat finished.")
+        return oracle_dir
